Subject: [PATCH] fix(entities): clear authoritative owner and attack targets

Translate explicit native reference clearing into Java metadata instead of
omitting the update and leaving the previous owner or attack target active.
Use the guardian hierarchy so elder guardians share the same target path.
Consolidate the three wither head translations while retaining their distinct
fields and full-width native actor identities.

BDS 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, sends guardian TARGET 0 after an
active negative unique ID and wither TARGET_A -1 after an active target.
The other wither heads initialize to -1, and an untamed wolf has OWNER -1.
Java 26.3 guardian and wither code uses integer zero for an absent target;
tameable ownership uses the existing nullable UUID serializer.

Sequence regressions fail before the fix. They cover binding, clearing,
restoration, large negative native IDs, elder guardians, all wither heads,
and owner replacement, including Java metadata encoding and decoding.
Late reference resolution and visible native/client comparisons remain
separate verification requirements.
